<title>CANADA: Western Canada rail car allocations for Sept 23.</title>
<headline>Western Canada rail car allocations for Sept 23.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Western Canada's Car</p>
<p>Allocation Policy Group on Monday issued its rail car</p>
<p>allocations by commodity for loading during shipping week nine</p>
<p>of the 1996/97 season, starting September 29.</p>
<p>VANCOUVER     1,800 cars</p>
<p>subtotal	1,206 CWB (wheat/barley)</p>
<p>		    582 canola</p>
<p>		     12 oats</p>
<p>PRINCE RUPERT 1,300 CWB THUNDER BAY   2,200 cars</p>
<p>subtotal	1,340 CWB</p>
<p>		    503 canola</p>
<p>		    163 oats</p>
<p>		    194 domestic feed wheat and barley</p>
<p>CHURCHILL	 300 CWB</p>
<p>-does not include U.S.-bound rail cars or interior domestic shipments.</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
</text>
